{{!-- The two desks in the dock, read off the site's own navigation
      so no extra query runs on every page. Two passes, so Technology
      is always first whatever order the menu is in.

      {{this.url}} and not {{url}}, and the difference is not cosmetic.
      url is a Ghost helper as well as a property name. As a bare
      mustache it calls the helper, which returns the URL of the
      resource in context; a navigation item is a plain object and not
      a resource, so the helper falls through to the current page and
      every desk link in the dock pointed at whatever page the reader
      was already on. Written as a path expression it reads the
      property, which is what is wanted.

      It works by accident in the footer, where the loop is over real
      tags and the helper happens to return the tag's own URL. --}}

{{#if @site.navigation}}
<nav class="lc-dock-nav" aria-label="Desks">
    {{#foreach @site.navigation}}{{#match this.url "~$" "/technology/"}}<a href="{{this.url}}" data-desk="technology">{{this.label}}</a>{{/match}}{{/foreach}}
    {{#foreach @site.navigation}}{{#match this.url "~$" "/philosophy/"}}<a href="{{this.url}}" data-desk="philosophy">{{this.label}}</a>{{/match}}{{/foreach}}
</nav>
{{/if}}
